Recorded answers from `kdos update check --json`, `kdos cve --json` and
`kdos-bootctl status`.

kdos-update computes none of the three: each is already answered by a program
in this tree, and a surface re-deriving a version comparison would be a second
answer that drifts. That makes its picture depend on the host's ports tree, its
package database and its boot state — none of which a golden may depend on, so
`KDOS_UPDATE_JSON`, `KDOS_CVE_JSON` and `KDOS_SLOT_TEXT` point at these.

The security table's own AGE is in cve.json on purpose: a table three months
stale reporting nothing to fix is worse than no answer, and the golden is what
proves the age reaches the screen.
